  "sections": [
    {
      "sectionId": "section-introduction",
      "heading": "Introduction",
      "sourceAnchor": "introduction",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-introduction-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "DnD 5.5’s "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "Tactical Combatant",
              "href": "https://www.dndbeyond.com/feats/2370869-tactical-combatant"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " feat, introduced in “"
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "D&D Beyond Drops",
              "href": "http://dndbeyond.com/drops"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "“, gives martial characters some useful options to protect themselves and support their skills. The features feel similar to the Fighter’s Second Wind and Tactical Mind features, providing durablity in combat and support for Ability Checks outside of combat."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-introduction-2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Ideal users for this feat are conventional martial characters using big weapons: Barbarians, Fighters, Paladins, and potentialy Rangers and Rogues if they’re using weapons like heavy crossbows and muskets which have big damage dice."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-ability-score-increase",
      "heading": "Ability Score Increase",
      "sourceAnchor": "ability-score-increase",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-ability-score-increase-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Perfect for conventional martial characters."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-buffering-strike",
      "heading": "Buffering Strike",
      "sourceAnchor": "buffering-strike",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-buffering-strike-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The Temporary Hit Points depend on the roll on your damage dice (not "
            },
            {
              "type": "emphasis",
              "text": "die"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ", notably), so you want a weapon with big damage dice like a greataxe or greatsword, and ideally you want to use this when you crit to maximize the value. But you can’t guarantee crits, so instead you may want damage reroll froms feats like Savage Attacker and Piercer."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-buffering-strike-2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "You can use the THP once per Short or Long Rest, but they last until you complete a Long Rest. If you’re about to rest and haven’t used this, grab your bag of rats so that you can come out of the rest with both Temporary Hit Points and with Buffering Strike ready to use."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-honed-instincts",
      "heading": "Honed Instincts",
      "sourceAnchor": "honed-instincts",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-honed-instincts-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Add a d6 to a failed Ability Check once per Short or Long Rest. Very similar to the Fighter’s Tactical Mind feature. If you have important skills (ex: Face skills on a Paladin) and don’t have magical support from spells like Enhance Ability, this can be great insurance."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-honed-instincts-2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "In the 2024 DnD 5.5 rules, many mechanics like this now only expend the use when the bonus die or reroll turns the failed check into a success. We’ve seen errata for other D&D Beyond Drops feats to make that change, so it’s possible that we’ll see the same for Tactical Combatant."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-5",
      "heading": "What are DnD Beyond Drops?",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-5-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Starting in April of 2026, DnD Beyond Drops aim to release monthly content for DnD 5.5 accessible exclusively to users with a paid subscription to DnD Beyond. The included character options are shareable with subscriptions that allow content sharing. For more information, see the official "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "D&D Beyond Drops FAQ",
              "href": "https://dndbeyond-support.wizards.com/hc/en-us/sections/48937182240404"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ". The developers also posted "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "Reddit AMA discussing Drops",
              "href": "https://www.reddit.com/r/dndbeyond/comments/1t6f0pe/ama_with_ddb_executive_producer_drops_product/"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " when they were announced."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-5-2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "We saw the first round of errata for Drops in "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "August of 2026",
              "href": "https://www.dndbeyond.com/posts/2222-d-d-beyonds-august-drop-sewers-and-treasures?icid_medium=organic&icid_source=homepage_drops&icid_campaign=2026_drops&icid_content=2026_hype"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ", so it appears that WotC plans to continue supporting Drops and to update the published content."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
